# playpick cell: mode=clear spec=rogue:assassination style=good size=25
# difficulty=heroic view=820x1180,touch save=carried (behaves as fresh, #273 --
# carried never actually carries across separate playbot invocations because
# the dev-server port is derived from the process pid).
#
# A fresh/carried save only opens Bonegrinder 10-normal by default, so
# #b=marrow&s=25&h=1 unlocks the whole chain up to 25-heroic before backing
# out to a real RAID -> WALK IN at the door (direction.md's 2026-09-26
# driver-lesson recipe).
#
# What no session has done before: rogue:assassination has been walked/cleared
# under melee, auto, idle and wander (direction.md's #6 thread), but never
# `good` -- the one style whose steering is an explicit beeline at a target,
# not a fixed heading or a random one. direction.md's #6 has already pinned
# rogue:assassination's own clean VIGIL crossings on its flat moveSpeed=178,
# the fastest in the roster, and separately found that `good`'s own beeline
# steering is what got a battleground body killed in under fifteen seconds on
# four separate specs (walking a body straight into a hostile cluster with no
# notion of how fragile it is). This cell is the first place both variables
# land on the same body at once: the fastest class in the roster, under the
# one style shown elsewhere to steer straight into danger, in a raid evening
# rather than a battleground -- where getting to the boss fast might cross
# corridors cleanly, or might carry the same walk-into-a-cluster habit into
# THE VIGIL's own watchmen and Bonegrinder heroic's bonestorm aura (#267,
# already measured as reversing melee's own hit ratio for a body that cannot
# leave its reach).
open #b=marrow&s=25&h=1
tap back
tap raid
tap next
tap class:rogue:assassination
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot start

evening good 200 8
state
shot end
says
bill
